he confluence of the White and Blue Nile.","verses":4,"v":[1]},{"id":"india_597","name":"India","kind":"Region","lat":22.0,"lon":77.0,"summary":"Occurs only in Esther 1:1 and 8:9, where the extent of the dominion of the Persian king is described. The country so designated here is not the peninsula of Hindustan, but the country surrounding the Indus, the Punjab.","verses":2,"v":[1]},{"id":"susa_1118","name":"Susa","kind":"City","lat":32.19202,"lon":48.24854,"summary":"A lily, the Susa of Greek and Roman writers, once the capital of Elam. It lay in the uplands of Susiana, on the east of the Tigris, about 150 miles to the north of the head of the Persian Gulf.","verses":20,"v":[2,5]},{"id":"media_776","name":"Media","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":34.5,"lon":46.5,"summary":"Heb. Madai, which is rendered in the Authorized Version (1) “Madai,” Gen. 10:2; (2) “Medes,” 2 Kings 17:6; 18:11; (3) “Media,” Esther 1:3; 10:2; Isa. 21:2; Dan. 8:20; (4) “Mede,” only in Dan. 11:1.","verses":8,"v":[3,14,18]},{"id":"persia_938","name":"Persia","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":34.79831,"lon":48.51497,"summary":"An ancient empire, extending from the Indus to Thrace, and from the Caspian Sea to the Red Sea and the Persian Gulf. The Persians were originally a Medic tribe which settled in Persia, on the eastern side of the Persian Gulf.","verses":25,"v":[3,14,18]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1961,1961,1961,1961,3117,3117,3117,325,325,4427,4427,4427,7651,4082,1912,1912,5704,3568],[1992,1992,3117,4428,325,3427,5921,4438,4438,3678,1002,1002,1002,7800,7800],[7969,7969,7969,8141,4427,4427,4427,6213,6213,4960,4960,3605,3605,8269,8269,5650,5650,2428,2428,2428,6539,6539,4074,4074,6440,6440,6579,6579,6579,6579,8269,8269,4082,4082,4082],[7227,7227,7227,7227,8084,3117,7200,7200,3519,3519,6239,4438,4438,4438,853,8597,8597,3366,1420,1420,1420],[4390,4390,4390,428,428,3117,1594,1594,1594,2691,4428,4428,4428,1055,4428,4428,6213,7651,7651,4960,3605,3605,5